Using a DocumentFragment is a high-performance optimization strategy because it acts as a lightweight, offscreen DOM container.
Adding elements to a regular DOM node one by one triggers expensive browser repaints and reflows for every single insertion. By assembling your nodes inside a DocumentFragment first, you perform all modifications in memory and trigger only one single reflow when you finally append the fragment to the live page.
