## Architectural Rules of DocumentFragments

* Auto-Emptying Mechanical Cleanups: Once you run .appendChild(fragment), the browser moves the internal child references out of the fragment completely. The DocumentFragment object remains in memory, but it becomes instantly completely empty and reusable.
* No Parent Anchorings: A DocumentFragment does not have a parentNode. It cannot accept style definitions or attributes directly on itself because it never physically exists inside the DOM render tree.

